-- chem/pathtransport.hypercubical — composing the edge holonomy along a path walks a charge from one end to the
-- other, one link at a time, so moving a charge a distance of k links takes exactly k holonomies. A single edge
-- holonomy transfers one unit of charge across one link (chem/edgehol.hypercubical). On a path v0 — v1 — v2 the
-- holonomy on the link nearer v2 moves the unit from v2 to v1, and the holonomy on the link nearer v0 moves it from
-- v1 to v0; applied in turn they carry the unit the full length, every intermediate vertex ending neutral. The
-- charge is moved the whole distance and the number of kinetic steps equals the separation: the discrete root of a
-- kinetic cost that grows with distance, where the electric energy does not (chem/pairenergy.hypercubical). Each
-- step's amplitude is the single-link hop; composing their costs along the path is the kinetic energy of separation.
import "edgehol.hypercubical"

